# 高频词汇 List02

## benefit
- **音标**: /ˈbenɪfɪt/
- **词性**: n. / v.
- **释义**: 利益；好处；有益于
- **例句**: Exercise has many health benefits.
- **近义词**: advantage, profit, gain
- **派生词**: beneficial (adj.), beneficiary (n.)

## bias
- **音标**: /ˈbaɪəs/
- **词性**: n. / v.
- **释义**: 偏见；使有偏见
- **例句**: The report showed a clear bias against the proposal.
- **近义词**: prejudice, partiality, favoritism
- **派生词**: biased (adj.), unbiased (adj.)

## capacity
- **音标**: /kəˈpæsəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 能力；容量；身份
- **例句**: The stadium has a capacity of 50,000.
- **近义词**: ability, volume, capability
- **派生词**: capacitate (v.)

## cease
- **音标**: /siːs/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 停止；终止
- **例句**: The factory ceased production last month.
- **近义词**: stop, halt, discontinue
- **派生词**: ceaseless (adj.), cessation (n.)

## challenge
- **音标**: /ˈtʃælɪndʒ/
- **词性**: n. / v.
- **释义**: 挑战；质疑
- **例句**: Climate change is a major challenge for humanity.
- **近义词**: dare, question, contest
- **派生词**: challenging (adj.), challenger (n.)

## circumstance
- **音标**: /ˈsɜːrkəmstæns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 环境；情况
- **例句**: Under no circumstances should you leave.
- **近义词**: situation, condition, context
- **派生词**: circumstantial (adj.)

## collapse
- **音标**: /kəˈlæps/
- **词性**: v. / n.
- **释义**: 倒塌；崩溃
- **例句**: The bridge collapsed during the earthquake.
- **近义词**: fall, crumble, break down
- **派生词**: collapsible (adj.)

## commission
- **音标**: /kəˈmɪʃn/
- **词性**: n. / v.
- **释义**: 委员会；佣金；委托
- **例句**: He earned a 10% commission on each sale.
- **近义词**: committee, fee, authorize
- **派生词**: commissioner (n.), commissioned (adj.)

## commit
- **音标**: /kəˈmɪt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 犯（罪）；承诺；投入
- **例句**: She committed herself to finishing the project.
- **近义词**: pledge, devote, perpetrate
- **派生词**: commitment (n.), committed (adj.)

## community
- **音标**: /kəˈmjuːnəti/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 社区；共同体
- **例句**: The local community raised funds for the school.
- **近义词**: society, neighborhood, public
- **派生词**: communal (adj.), communicate (v.)

## comprehensive
- **音标**: /ˌkɒmprɪˈhensɪv/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 全面的；综合的
- **例句**: The report provides a comprehensive analysis.
- **近义词**: thorough, complete, extensive
- **派生词**: comprehensively (adv.), comprehension (n.)

## conclude
- **音标**: /kənˈkluːd/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 结束；得出结论
- **例句**: The study concluded that exercise improves memory.
- **近义词**: finish, determine, infer
- **派生词**: conclusion (n.), conclusive (adj.)

## conduct
- **音标**: /kənˈdʌkt/
- **词性**: v. / n.
- **释义**: 进行；行为；指挥
- **例句**: The scientist conducted an experiment.
- **近义词**: perform, behavior, carry out
- **派生词**: conductor (n.), conductive (adj.)

## confirm
- **音标**: /kənˈfɜːrm/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 确认；证实
- **例句**: Please confirm your reservation by email.
- **近义词**: verify, validate, affirm
- **派生词**: confirmation (n.), confirmed (adj.)

## conflict
- **音标**: /ˈkɒnflɪkt/
- **词性**: n. / v.
- **释义**: 冲突；矛盾
- **例句**: There is a conflict between work and family life.
- **近义词**: clash, struggle, disagreement
- **派生词**: conflicting (adj.)

## consequence
- **音标**: /ˈkɒnsɪkwəns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 后果；重要性
- **例句**: He must face the consequences of his actions.
- **近义词**: result, outcome, effect
- **派生词**: consequently (adv.), consequential (adj.)

## considerable
- **音标**: /kənˈsɪdərəbl/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 相当大的；值得考虑的
- **例句**: A considerable amount of money was spent on research.
- **近义词**: significant, substantial, sizable
- **派生词**: considerably (adv.)

## consistent
- **音标**: /kənˈsɪstənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 一致的；始终如一的
- **例句**: Her work has been consistent throughout the year.
- **近义词**: steady, constant, uniform
- **派生词**: consistency (n.), inconsistently (adv.)

## constitute
- **音标**: /ˈkɒnstɪtjuːt/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 构成；组成
- **例句**: Women constitute 60% of the workforce.
- **近义词**: compose, form, make up
- **派生词**: constitution (n.), constitutional (adj.)

## consume
- **音标**: /kənˈsjuːm/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 消耗；消费；吃
- **例句**: The project consumed all his energy.
- **近义词**: use up, devour, deplete
- **派生词**: consumer (n.), consumption (n.)
